-- ============================================================================
-- migration-checksum-origin.sql
--
-- Read-only Production evidence: the ORIGIN of the ledger's checksum differences.
--
-- Run 40625984917 (accountant-ops-ledger-names.sql) found 59 finished ledger rows whose checksum differs from the
-- migration.sql on main. This file explains each of them, without changing anything. For every migration directory
-- on main at c7d4531f (201 names) it embeds, from the git blobs:
--   current_lf    the sha256 of today's file (LF, as in git);
--   current_crlf  the same bytes with CRLF line endings (a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf);
--   earlier_lf / earlier_crlf  every EARLIER version of the file in git history (the 6 files edited after
--                 they were added: 6 earlier versions), as LF and as CRLF.
-- Each mismatching ledger row is classified by the FIRST of those its checksum equals, else "unexplained" —
-- separately for the files edited after creation and for the others.
--
-- OUTPUT: n | flag | observed_count; a second listing counts unexplained rows by month (yyyymm), numbers only.
-- PRIVACY: the ledger only (schema metadata). Guard-clean: no write keyword anywhere, prose included.
-- ============================================================================

\echo '== migration checksum origin: legend (n -> check) =='
\echo ' 1 the evidence role is a superuser or has BYPASSRLS (flag)'
\echo ' 2 finished ledger rows that are a migration on main (count)'
\echo ' 3 …whose checksum equals today''s file, LF (count)'
\echo ' 4 …whose checksum differs from today''s file (count; run 40625984917 saw 59)'
\echo ' 5 files NOT edited after creation: mismatching rows (count)'
\echo ' 6 …explained by CRLF line endings of the same file (count)'
\echo ' 7 …unexplained (count)'
\echo ' 8 files edited after creation (6 files): mismatching rows (count)'
\echo ' 9 …explained by today''s file with CRLF (count)'
\echo '10 …explained by an earlier version, LF (count)'
\echo '11 …explained by an earlier version, CRLF (count)'
\echo '12 …unexplained (count)'
\echo '13 every mismatch is explained (flag; t when 7 + 12 = 0)'
\echo '14 the three G5 migrations (20261107090000 / 091000 / 092000) have no ledger row (count; expected 0)'

